# SRG-APP-000745-WSR-000120  -  CAT II
# The web server must implement the capability to centrally review and
# analyze audit records from multiple components within the system.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000745-WSR-000120
group:           V-264339
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003821
control_rev5:    AU-6

contribution:    Splunk Web is the application's own review and analysis interface, served
                 by the same instance; the application enables that interface and sets the
                 breadth of records the reviewing role can reach through it.

governs:         authorize.conf - Used to create roles.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           authorize.conf [role_<roleName>] srchIndexesAllowed non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] startwebserver https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] startwebserver equals 1
                 reason: "startwebserver = [0 | 1]. Set whether or not to start Splunk Web.
                         0 disables Splunk Web, 1 enables it. Default: 1"
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The scope of coverage the interface must reach is organization-defined and
                 recorded in the site security plan, per product STIG SPLK-CL-000100.
external:        Reaching Splunk Web from an analyst workstation depends on network access
                 and on the host firewall, which are not application settings.
external:        Where the indexers are separate instances, distsearch.conf
                 [distributedSearch] servers must name them; a single-instance deployment
                 has no search peers and their absence is not a finding.

citation:        web.conf.spec:16 [settings], :23 startwebserver = [0 | 1] default 1;
                 authorize.conf.spec:67 [role_<roleName>], :292 srchIndexesAllowed;
                 distsearch.conf.spec:29, :81 servers. Product STIG SPLK-CL-000100.
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: Splunk Web is disabled, or the
                 role that performs audit review is not allowed to search the indexes
                 holding the aggregated records, so the application's own central review
                 interface cannot reach audit records from multiple components.
